\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


An additive randomized encoding locally maps each party\textquotesingle s input into group elements whose aggregate permits decoding the desired output while hiding additional input information. Computational privacy is indistinguishability from a simulator based on the prescribed output.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
